@math{{\it Bernoulli}(p)}
@end iftex 
random variable, with @math{0 \leq p \leq 1}.

The 
@html
\({\it Bernoulli}(p)\)
@end html
@ifinfo
@math{Bernoulli(p)}
@end ifinfo
@iftex
@math{{\it Bernoulli}(p)}
@end iftex 
random variable is equivalent to the 
@html
\({\it Binomial}(1,p)\)
@end html
@ifinfo
@math{Binomial(1,p)}
@end ifinfo
@iftex
@math{{\it Binomial}(1,p)}
@end iftex
.

The mean is
@html
$$
f(x; p) = p^x (1-p)^{1-x}
$$
@end html
@ifinfo

@example
                                       1 - x  x
                      f(x, p) = (1 - p)      p
@end example


@end ifinfo
@tex
$$f(x; p) = p^x (1-p)^{1-x}$$
@end tex


